  "content": {
    "id": "p16-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "If $a$ and 35 are coprime, then prove that $a^{12}\\equiv1\\pmod{35}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a^{12}\\equiv1\\pmod{35}$.\n\nFermat’s Little Theorem gives the result modulo both 7 and 5; their coprimality gives the result modulo 35.",
      "worked": "Since $\\gcd(a,35)=1$, neither 7 nor 5 divides $a$. By Fermat’s Little Theorem,\n$$\\begin{align*}a^6&\\equiv1\\pmod7,\\\\a^{12}&=(a^6)^2,\\\\a^{12}&\\equiv1\\pmod7.\\end{align*}$$\nAlso,\n$$\\begin{align*}a^4&\\equiv1\\pmod5,\\\\a^{12}&=(a^4)^3,\\\\a^{12}&\\equiv1\\pmod5.\\end{align*}$$\nThus both 7 and 5 divide $a^{12}-1$. Since $\\gcd(7,5)=1$, their product 35 divides $a^{12}-1$. Hence $a^{12}\\equiv1\\pmod{35}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 55
  },
